#[Page('/components/combobox')]
function ComboboxPage(): Node
{
    return (
        <DemoPage slug="combobox">
            <Hero source="ComboboxHeroDemo">
                <ComboboxHeroDemo />
            </Hero>
            <Examples>
                <Example title="Value selection with IDs" source="ComboboxIdsDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>When your app stores IDs rather than labels, give each <code>ComboboxItem</code> the ID as its <code>value</code>, and the label as its content. With <code>selectionMode="single"</code>, the input shows the label, and the form gets the ID.</p>
                        <p>The label is also used for filtering and typeahead.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ComboboxIdsDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Multiple select" source="ComboboxMultipleDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>The combobox can allow multiple selections by adding the <code>multiple</code> prop to <code>Combobox</code>. Selection chips are rendered with <code>ComboboxChip</code> inside the input that can be removed. Render a chip with the <code>value</code> of each item: the browser keeps the selection, and shows the chips of the chosen items.</p>
                        <p>In order for screen readers to announce how to reach and remove the chips, add <code>aria-description</code> to <code>ComboboxChip</code> and <code>selectedDescription</code> to <code>ComboboxInput</code>, alongside the <code>aria-label</code> on <code>ComboboxChips</code> and <code>ComboboxChipRemove</code>. Translate them together with the rest of your interface.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ComboboxMultipleDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Input inside popup" source="ComboboxInputInsidePopupDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p><code>ComboboxInput</code> can be rendered inside <code>ComboboxPopup</code> to create a searchable select popup. The trigger shows the value with <code>ComboboxValue</code>.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ComboboxInputInsidePopupDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Grouped" source="ComboboxGroupedDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Organize related options with <code>ComboboxGroup</code> and <code>ComboboxGroupLabel</code> to add section headings inside the popup.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ComboboxGroupedDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Async search (single)" source="ComboboxAsyncSingleDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Load items from the server on input changes: the <code>onChange</code> handler of <code>ComboboxInput</code> calls a repository service, and the state keeps the results. With <code>phem:bind</code> on the root, the browser keeps the selection and the selected item in the list. <code>ComboboxStatus</code> shows the texts of the states of the search: <code>pending</code> with a spinner while it runs, <code>error</code> when the handler throws, <code>idle</code> before the user types, and <code>empty</code> when nothing matches. This pattern avoids needing to load items upfront.</p>
                        <p>The <code>onClick</code> handler of an item assigns the person. The selection shows at once, and the clear button shows a spinner until the server answers. When the handler fails, the button shows a warning, and after one second the selection goes. Choose Marvin McKinney to see a failure.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ComboboxAsyncSingleDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Async search (multiple)" source="ComboboxAsyncMultipleDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Load items from the server on input changes while supporting multiple selections. Give each <code>ComboboxChip</code> the <code>value</code> of its item: the browser keeps the chosen items in the list while new matches come in. The handler of an item adds or removes the person, and a choice with a text closes the popup and clears the text. This pattern avoids needing to load items upfront.</p>
                        <p>A choice shows at once: the browser adds a chip from <code>ComboboxChipTemplate</code>, where <code>{label}</code> is the label of the item, and its remove button shows a spinner until the server answers. When the handler fails, the button shows a warning, and after one second the chip goes. Choose Marvin McKinney to see a failure.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ComboboxAsyncMultipleDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Async search in a form" source="ComboboxAsyncFormDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Load items from the server on input changes, and send the choices with the form. Give the root a <code>name</code> and a <code>selectionMode</code> (<code>single</code>, or <code>multiple</code> with <code>multiple</code>), and the items no <code>onClick</code> handler: the browser keeps the selection, and a choice sends no event. With <code>multiple</code>, the browser adds a chip from <code>ComboboxChipTemplate</code> for each choice, and each chip has a hidden input with the value of its item. The <code>onSubmit</code> handler of the form gets the values.</p>
                        <p>Use this pattern when the app saves all the data of a form on submit. Use the async search examples above when each choice saves at once.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ComboboxAsyncFormDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Creatable" source="ComboboxCreatableDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Create a new item when the filter matches no items, opening a creation <a href="/components/dialog" className="underline">Dialog</a>.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ComboboxCreatableDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Large datasets" source="ComboboxLargeDatasetDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>For a large dataset, render only the first matches in the popup, and show the total in the status. The server searches the dataset at each change of the input.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ComboboxLargeDatasetDemo />
                </Example>
            </Examples>
        </DemoPage>
    );
}

#[Component]
function ComboboxHeroDemo(): Node
{
    $fruits = FRUITS;

    return (
        <Combobox id="fruit" filter="contains">
            <ComboboxLabel>Choose a fruit</ComboboxLabel>
            <ComboboxInputGroup>
                <ComboboxInput placeholder="e.g. Apple" />
                <ComboboxActions>
                    <ComboboxClear aria-label="Clear selection" />
                    <ComboboxTrigger aria-label="Open popup" />
                </ComboboxActions>
            </ComboboxInputGroup>
            <ComboboxPopup>
                <ComboboxEmpty>No fruits found.</ComboboxEmpty>
                <ComboboxList>
                    {% for value, label in fruits %}
                        <ComboboxItem key={{ value }} value={{ value }}>
                            <ComboboxItemIndicator />
                            <ComboboxItemLabel>{{ label }}</ComboboxItemLabel>
                        </ComboboxItem>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ComboboxList>
            </ComboboxPopup>
        </Combobox>
    );
}

#[Component]
function ComboboxIdsDemo(): Node
{
    $fruits = FRUITS;

    return (
        <Combobox id="fruit-ids" filter="contains" selectionMode="single" defaultValue="banana" name="fruit">
            <ComboboxLabel>Choose a fruit</ComboboxLabel>
            <ComboboxInputGroup>
                <ComboboxInput placeholder="e.g. Apple" />
                <ComboboxActions>
                    <ComboboxClear aria-label="Clear selection" />
                    <ComboboxTrigger aria-label="Open popup" />
                </ComboboxActions>
            </ComboboxInputGroup>
            <ComboboxPopup>
                <ComboboxEmpty>No fruits found.</ComboboxEmpty>
                <ComboboxList>
                    {% for value, label in fruits %}
                        <ComboboxItem key={{ value }} value={{ value }}>
                            <ComboboxItemIndicator />
                            <ComboboxItemLabel>{{ label }}</ComboboxItemLabel>
                        </ComboboxItem>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ComboboxList>
            </ComboboxPopup>
        </Combobox>
    );
}

// The browser keeps the chosen languages: a click on an item shows its chip, with no
// event of the server.
#[Component]
function ComboboxMultipleDemo(): Node
{
    $languages = [
        'js' => 'JavaScript',
        'ts' => 'TypeScript',
        'py' => 'Python',
        'java' => 'Java',
        'cpp' => 'C++',
        'cs' => 'C#',
        'php' => 'PHP',
        'ruby' => 'Ruby',
        'go' => 'Go',
        'rust' => 'Rust',
        'swift' => 'Swift',
    ];

    return (
        <Combobox id="languages" multiple filter="contains" className="max-w-md">
            <ComboboxLabel>Programming languages</ComboboxLabel>
            <ComboboxInputGroup>
                <ComboboxChips aria-label="Selected languages">
                    {% for id, label in languages %}
                        <ComboboxChip key={{ id }} value={{ id }} aria-label={{ label }}>
                            {{ label }}
                            <ComboboxChipRemove aria-label="Remove {{ label }}" />
                        </ComboboxChip>
                    {% endfor %}
                    <ComboboxInput placeholder="e.g. TypeScript" selectedDescription="{count} selected. From the start of the input, press Left Arrow to focus the selected items" />
                </ComboboxChips>
            </ComboboxInputGroup>
            <ComboboxPopup className="duration-150">
                <ComboboxEmpty className="py-2">No languages found.</ComboboxEmpty>
                <ComboboxList className="max-h-[min(var(--available-height),24.5rem)] scroll-py-0 data-empty:py-1">
                    {% for id, label in languages %}
                        <ComboboxItem key={{ id }} value={{ id }}>
                            <ComboboxItemIndicator />
                            <ComboboxItemLabel>{{ label }}</ComboboxItemLabel>
                        </ComboboxItem>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ComboboxList>
            </ComboboxPopup>
        </Combobox>
    );
}

#[Component]
function ComboboxGroupedDemo(): Node
{
    $groups = [
        'Fruits' => [
            'Apple',
            'Banana',
            'Mango',
            'Kiwi',
            'Grape',
            'Orange',
            'Strawberry',
            'Watermelon',
        ],
        'Vegetables' => [
            'Broccoli',
            'Carrot',
            'Cauliflower',
            'Cucumber',
            'Kale',
            'Bell pepper',
            'Spinach',
            'Zucchini',
        ],
    ];

    return (
        <Combobox id="produce" filter="contains">
            <ComboboxLabel>Select produce</ComboboxLabel>
            <ComboboxInputGroup className="w-64">
                <ComboboxInput placeholder="e.g. Mango" />
                <ComboboxActions>
                    <ComboboxClear aria-label="Clear selection" />
                    <ComboboxTrigger aria-label="Open popup" />
                </ComboboxActions>
            </ComboboxInputGroup>
            <ComboboxPopup>
                <ComboboxEmpty>No produce found.</ComboboxEmpty>
                <ComboboxList>
                    {% for name, items in groups %}
                        <ComboboxGroup key={{ name }} className="block pb-2 last:pb-0">
                            <ComboboxGroupLabel className="pr-2 pl-8">{{ name }}</ComboboxGroupLabel>
                            {% for label in items %}
                                <ComboboxItem key={{ label }} value={{ label|lower|replace({' ': '-'}) }}>
                                    <ComboboxItemIndicator />
                                    <ComboboxItemLabel>{{ label }}</ComboboxItemLabel>
                                </ComboboxItem>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </ComboboxGroup>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ComboboxList>
            </ComboboxPopup>
        </Combobox>
    );
}

#[Component]
function ComboboxInputInsidePopupDemo(): Node
{
    $countries = COUNTRIES;

    return (
        <Combobox id="country" filter="contains" selectionMode="single" align={{ Align.Start }} className="items-start">
            <ComboboxLabel id="country-label" className="cursor-default text-sm leading-5 font-bold text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">Country</ComboboxLabel>
            <ComboboxTrigger tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="country-label" className="h-8 w-auto min-w-40 cursor-default justify-between gap-3 border border-neutral-950 bg-white pl-2 pr-1 text-sm leading-none whitespace-nowrap font-normal select-none hover:bg-neutral-100 active:bg-neutral-200 data-pressed:bg-neutral-100 data-placeholder:text-neutral-500 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:-outline-offset-1 focus-visible:outline-neutral-950 dark:data-placeholder:text-neutral-400 dark:focus-visible:outline-white dark:border-white dark:bg-neutral-950 dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 dark:active:bg-neutral-700 dark:data-pressed:bg-neutral-800">
                <ComboboxValue placeholder="Select country" />
                <ComboboxIcon />
            </ComboboxTrigger>
            <ComboboxPopup aria-label="Select country" className="w-auto border-0 [--input-container-height:2rem] max-h-[24.5rem] duration-150 data-starting-style:scale-90 data-ending-style:scale-90">
                <ComboboxInput placeholder="e.g. United Kingdom" className="w-full min-w-80 focus:-outline-offset-2" />
                <div className="border-x border-b border-neutral-950 dark:border-white">
                    <ComboboxEmpty>No countries found.</ComboboxEmpty>
                    <ComboboxList className="max-h-[min(calc(24.5rem-var(--input-container-height)-2px),calc(var(--available-height)-var(--input-container-height)-2px))] overflow-auto empty:p-0">
                        {% for code, label in countries %}
                            <ComboboxItem key={{ code }} value={{ code }}>
                                <ComboboxItemIndicator />
                                <ComboboxItemLabel>{{ label }}</ComboboxItemLabel>
                            </ComboboxItem>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </ComboboxList>
                </div>
            </ComboboxPopup>
        </Combobox>
    );
}

// The search runs in the handler of the input, as the Async search of Base UI: the repository
// searches, and the state keeps the results. The browser keeps the selection and the selected
// person in the list, and the root binds the selected value. The handler of an item assigns the
// person: the selection shows before the answer, and goes when the assignment fails.
#[Component]
final class ComboboxAsyncSingleDemo
{
    #[State] public string $query = '';
    #[State] public string $selected = '';
    /** @var list<array<string, string>> */
    #[State] public array $people = [];

    public function __construct(private readonly PersonRepository $repository)
    {
    }

    public function search(Event $e): void
    {
        $this->query = trim((string) $e->value);
        $this->people = $this->repository->search($this->query);
    }

    public function assign(string $id): void
    {
        $this->selected = $this->repository->assign($id)['id'];
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        return (
            <Combobox id="reviewer" phem:bind={{ selected }}>
                <ComboboxLabel>Assign reviewer</ComboboxLabel>
                <ComboboxInputGroup className="w-64 md:w-80">
                    <ComboboxInput onChange={{ search }} placeholder="e.g. Michael" />
                    <ComboboxActions>
                        <ComboboxClear aria-label="Clear selection" />
                        <ComboboxTrigger aria-label="Open popup" />
                    </ComboboxActions>
                </ComboboxInputGroup>
                <ComboboxPopup className="py-1">
                    <ComboboxStatus
                        idle="Start typing to search people…"
                        pending="Searching…"
                        empty={{ 'No matches for "' ~ query ~ '".' }}
                        error="Failed to fetch people. Please try again."
                    />
                    <ComboboxEmpty className="py-2">Try a different search term.</ComboboxEmpty>
                    <ComboboxList className="py-0">
                        {% for person in people %}
                            <ComboboxItem key={{ person.id }} value={{ person.id }} label={{ person.name }} onClick={{ assign(person.id) }} className="items-start leading-[1.2rem] data-highlighted:text-neutral-950 data-highlighted:before:bg-neutral-100 dark:data-highlighted:text-white dark:data-highlighted:before:bg-neutral-800">
                                <ComboboxItemIndicator className="mt-1" />
                                <span className="col-start-2 flex flex-col gap-1">
                                    <span className="text-sm leading-5 font-bold">{{ person.name }}</span>
                                    <span className="text-xs">{{ person.email }}</span>
                                    <span className="flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-xs text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
                                        <span>@{{ person.username }}</span>
                                        <span>{{ person.title }}</span>
                                    </span>
                                </span>
                            </ComboboxItem>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </ComboboxList>
                </ComboboxPopup>
            </Combobox>
        );
    }
}

// The search of the server with more than one choice, as the Async search of Base UI: the chips
// show the chosen people, and the browser keeps their items in the list. A choice with a text
// closes the popup, and the text goes. The browser adds the chip of a new choice at once, from
// the template, and removes it when the assignment fails.
#[Component]
final class ComboboxAsyncMultipleDemo
{
    #[State] public string $query = '';
    /** @var list<array<string, string>> */
    #[State] public array $people = [];
    /** @var list<array<string, string>> */
    #[State] public array $chosen = [];

    public function __construct(private readonly PersonRepository $repository)
    {
    }

    public function search(Event $e): void
    {
        $this->query = trim((string) $e->value);
        $this->people = $this->repository->search($this->query);
    }

    public function toggle(string $id): void
    {
        $others = array_values(array_filter($this->chosen, static fn (array $person): bool => $person['id'] !== $id));
        $this->chosen = $others !== $this->chosen ? $others : [...$this->chosen, $this->repository->assign($id)];
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        $count = \count($this->chosen);

        return (
            <Combobox id="reviewers" multiple className="max-w-md">
                <ComboboxLabel>Assign reviewers</ComboboxLabel>
                <ComboboxInputGroup>
                    <ComboboxChips aria-label={{ count > 0 ? 'Selected reviewers' : null }}>
                        {% for person in chosen %}
                            <ComboboxChip key={{ person.id }} value={{ person.id }} aria-label={{ person.name }}>
                                {{ person.name }}
                                <ComboboxChipRemove aria-label="Remove {{ person.name }}" onClick={{ toggle(person.id) }} />
                            </ComboboxChip>
                        {% endfor %}
                        <ComboboxChipTemplate>
                            <ComboboxChip aria-label="{label}">
                                {label}
                                <ComboboxChipRemove aria-label="Remove {label}" />
                            </ComboboxChip>
                        </ComboboxChipTemplate>
                        <ComboboxInput
                            onChange={{ search }}
                            placeholder={{ count > 0 ? '' : 'e.g. Michael' }}
                            aria-description={{ count > 0 ? count ~ ' selected. From the start of the input, press Left Arrow to focus the selected items' : null }}
                        />
                    </ComboboxChips>
                </ComboboxInputGroup>
                <ComboboxPopup className="py-1">
                    <ComboboxStatus
                        idle="Start typing to search people…"
                        pending="Searching…"
                        empty={{ 'No matches for "' ~ query ~ '".' }}
                        error="Failed to fetch people. Please try again."
                    />
                    <ComboboxEmpty className="py-2">Try a different search term.</ComboboxEmpty>
                    <ComboboxList className="max-h-[min(24.5rem,var(--available-height))] py-0">
                        {% for person in people %}
                            <ComboboxItem key={{ person.id }} value={{ person.id }} label={{ person.name }} selected={{ person.id in chosen|column('id') }} onClick={{ toggle(person.id) }} className="items-start leading-[1.2rem] data-highlighted:text-neutral-950 data-highlighted:before:bg-neutral-100 dark:data-highlighted:text-white dark:data-highlighted:before:bg-neutral-800">
                                <ComboboxItemIndicator className="mt-1" />
                                <span className="col-start-2 flex flex-col gap-1">
                                    <span className="text-sm leading-5 font-bold">{{ person.name }}</span>
                                    <span className="text-xs">{{ person.email }}</span>
                                    <span className="flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-xs text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
                                        <span>@{{ person.username }}</span>
                                        <span>{{ person.title }}</span>
                                    </span>
                                </span>
                            </ComboboxItem>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </ComboboxList>
                </ComboboxPopup>
            </Combobox>
        );
    }
}

// The search of the server in a form: the browser keeps the choices, and the submit sends them.
// The items have no handler, so a choice sends no event, and the `selectionMode` of each root gives
// the selection to the browser. The `name` of each root gives the form its values: the hidden input of the owner, and the hidden input of each chip of a reviewer.
#[Component]
final class ComboboxAsyncFormDemo
{
    #[State] public string $ownerQuery = '';
    #[State] public string $reviewersQuery = '';
    /** @var list<array<string, string>> */
    #[State] public array $owners = [];
    /** @var list<array<string, string>> */
    #[State] public array $reviewers = [];
    /** @var array<string, string> */
    #[State] public array $errors = [];
    #[State] public ?string $result = null;

    public function __construct(private readonly PersonRepository $repository)
    {
    }

    public function searchOwners(Event $e): void
    {
        $this->ownerQuery = trim((string) $e->value);
        $this->owners = $this->repository->search($this->ownerQuery);
    }

    public function searchReviewers(Event $e): void
    {
        $this->reviewersQuery = trim((string) $e->value);
        $this->reviewers = $this->repository->search($this->reviewersQuery);
    }

    public function save(Event $e): void
    {
        // The browser sends the values: an id that is not a person is not a choice.
        $owner = $this->repository->find((string) ($e->form['owner'] ?? ''));
        $reviewers = array_filter(array_map(fn (mixed $id): ?array => $this->repository->find((string) $id), (array) ($e->form['reviewers'] ?? [])));

        $this->errors = array_filter([
            'owner' => null === $owner ? 'Choose an owner.' : null,
            'reviewers' => [] === $reviewers ? 'Choose at least one reviewer.' : null,
        ]);
        if ([] !== $this->errors) {
            $this->result = null;

            return;
        }

        $this->result = 'Owner: '.$owner['name'].'. Reviewers: '.implode(', ', array_column($reviewers, 'name')).'.';
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        return (
            <form onSubmit={{ save }} className="flex flex-col items-start gap-4">
                <div className="flex flex-col gap-1">
                    <Combobox id="form-owner" name="owner" selectionMode="single">
                        <ComboboxLabel>Owner</ComboboxLabel>
                        <ComboboxInputGroup className="w-64 md:w-80">
                            <ComboboxInput onChange={{ searchOwners }} placeholder="e.g. Michael" aria-invalid={{ errors.owner is defined ? 'true' : null }} aria-describedby={{ errors.owner is defined ? 'form-owner-error' : null }} />
                            <ComboboxActions>
                                <ComboboxClear aria-label="Clear selection" />
                                <ComboboxTrigger aria-label="Open popup" />
                            </ComboboxActions>
                        </ComboboxInputGroup>
                        <ComboboxPopup className="py-1">
                            <ComboboxStatus
                                idle="Start typing to search people…"
                                pending="Searching…"
                                empty={{ 'No matches for "' ~ ownerQuery ~ '".' }}
                                error="Failed to fetch people. Please try again."
                            />
                            <ComboboxList className="py-0">
                                {% for person in owners %}
                                    <ComboboxItem key={{ person.id }} value={{ person.id }} label={{ person.name }}>
                                        <ComboboxItemIndicator />
                                        <ComboboxItemLabel>{{ person.name }}</ComboboxItemLabel>
                                    </ComboboxItem>
                                {% endfor %}
                            </ComboboxList>
                        </ComboboxPopup>
                    </Combobox>
                    {% if errors.owner is defined %}<p id="form-owner-error" className="text-sm text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">{{ errors.owner }}</p>{% endif %}
                </div>
                <div className="flex flex-col gap-1">
                    <Combobox id="form-reviewers" name="reviewers" multiple selectionMode="multiple" className="max-w-md">
                        <ComboboxLabel>Reviewers</ComboboxLabel>
                        <ComboboxInputGroup>
                            <ComboboxChips aria-label="Selected reviewers">
                                <ComboboxChipTemplate>
                                    <ComboboxChip aria-label="{label}">
                                        {label}
                                        <ComboboxChipRemove aria-label="Remove {label}" />
                                    </ComboboxChip>
                                </ComboboxChipTemplate>
                                <ComboboxInput
                                    onChange={{ searchReviewers }}
                                    placeholder="e.g. Michael"
                                    selectedDescription="{count} selected. From the start of the input, press Left Arrow to focus the selected items"
                                    aria-invalid={{ errors.reviewers is defined ? 'true' : null }}
                                    aria-describedby={{ errors.reviewers is defined ? 'form-reviewers-error' : null }}
                                />
                            </ComboboxChips>
                        </ComboboxInputGroup>
                        <ComboboxPopup className="py-1">
                            <ComboboxStatus
                                idle="Start typing to search people…"
                                pending="Searching…"
                                empty={{ 'No matches for "' ~ reviewersQuery ~ '".' }}
                                error="Failed to fetch people. Please try again."
                            />
                            <ComboboxList className="max-h-[min(24.5rem,var(--available-height))] py-0">
                                {% for person in reviewers %}
                                    <ComboboxItem key={{ person.id }} value={{ person.id }} label={{ person.name }}>
                                        <ComboboxItemIndicator />
                                        <ComboboxItemLabel>{{ person.name }}</ComboboxItemLabel>
                                    </ComboboxItem>
                                {% endfor %}
                            </ComboboxList>
                        </ComboboxPopup>
                    </Combobox>
                    {% if errors.reviewers is defined %}<p id="form-reviewers-error" className="text-sm text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">{{ errors.reviewers }}</p>{% endif %}
                </div>
                <Button type="submit">Submit</Button>
                <p role="status" className="text-sm empty:hidden">{{ result }}</p>
            </form>
        );
    }
}

// The labels of the Creatable demo of Base UI. A text that matches no label shows a
// "Create" item, which opens a dialog to name the new label. The "Create" item runs a
// handler, so the server keeps the chosen labels (`selectionMode="none"`).
#[Component]
final class ComboboxCreatableDemo
{
    /** @var array<string, string> */
    #[State] public array $labels = [
        'bug' => 'bug',
        'docs' => 'documentation',
        'enhancement' => 'enhancement',
        'help-wanted' => 'help wanted',
        'good-first-issue' => 'good first issue',
    ];
    /** @var list<string> */
    #[State] public array $selected = [];
    #[State] public string $query = '';
    #[State] public ?string $creating = null;

    public function toggle(string $id): void
    {
        $this->selected = \in_array($id, $this->selected, true)
            ? array_values(array_diff($this->selected, [$id]))
            : [...$this->selected, $id];
        $this->query = '';
    }

    public function remove(string $id): void
    {
        $this->selected = array_values(array_diff($this->selected, [$id]));
    }

    public function startCreate(): void
    {
        $this->creating = trim($this->query);
    }

    public function create(Event $e): void
    {
        $value = trim((string) ($e->form['label'] ?? ''));
        $this->creating = null;
        $this->query = '';
        if ('' === $value) {
            return;
        }

        $existing = array_search(
            mb_strtolower($value),
            array_map(mb_strtolower(...), $this->labels),
            true,
        );
        if (false !== $existing) {
            $this->selected = array_values(
                array_unique([...$this->selected, (string) $existing]),
            );

            return;
        }

        $id = $base = preg_replace('/\s+/', '-', mb_strtolower($value));
        for ($i = 2; isset($this->labels[$id]); ++$i) {
            $id = $base.'-'.$i;
        }
        $this->labels[$id] = $value;
        $this->selected[] = $id;
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        $trimmed = trim($this->query);
        $exists = \in_array(
            mb_strtolower($trimmed),
            array_map(mb_strtolower(...), $this->labels),
            true,
        );
        $creatable = '' !== $trimmed && !$exists;
        $count = \count($this->selected);
        $open = null !== $this->creating;

        return (
            <div className="contents">
                <Combobox id="labels" multiple filter="contains" selectionMode="none">
                    <ComboboxLabel>Labels</ComboboxLabel>
                    <ComboboxInputGroup>
                        <ComboboxChips aria-label={{ count > 0 ? 'Selected labels' : null }}>
                            {% for id in selected %}
                                <ComboboxChip key={{ id }} aria-label={{ labels[id] }}>
                                    {{ labels[id] }}
                                    <ComboboxChipRemove aria-label="Remove {{ labels[id] }}" onClick={{ remove(id) }} />
                                </ComboboxChip>
                            {% endfor %}
                            <ComboboxInput phem:bind={{ query }} placeholder={{ count > 0 ? '' : 'e.g. bug' }} />
                        </ComboboxChips>
                    </ComboboxInputGroup>
                    <ComboboxPopup>
                        <ComboboxEmpty>No labels found.</ComboboxEmpty>
                        <ComboboxList>
                            {% for id, label in labels %}
                                <ComboboxItem key={{ id }} value={{ id }} selected={{ id in selected }} onClick={{ toggle(id) }}>
                                    <ComboboxItemIndicator />
                                    <ComboboxItemLabel>{{ label }}</ComboboxItemLabel>
                                </ComboboxItem>
                            {% endfor %}
                            {% if creatable %}
                                <ComboboxItem key="create" value="create" data-label={{ trimmed }} onClick={{ startCreate }}>
                                    <span className="col-start-2">Create "{{ trimmed }}"</span>
                                </ComboboxItem>
                            {% endif %}
                        </ComboboxList>
                    </ComboboxPopup>
                </Combobox>
                <Dialog defaultOpen={{ open }}>
                    <DialogPopup>
                        <DialogTitle>Create new label</DialogTitle>
                        <DialogDescription>Add a new label to select.</DialogDescription>
                        <form onSubmit={{ create }} className="flex flex-col gap-4">
                            <input name="label" aria-label="Label name" placeholder="Label name" value={{ creating }} autofocus className="h-8 w-full border border-neutral-950 bg-white px-2 text-sm dark:border-white dark:bg-neutral-950" />
                            <div className="flex justify-end gap-3">
                                <DialogClose>Cancel</DialogClose>
                                <Button type="submit">Create</Button>
                            </div>
                        </form>
                    </DialogPopup>
                </Dialog>
            </div>
        );
    }
}

// 10,000 items: the server finds the matches, and renders the first 50 of them.
#[Component]
final class ComboboxLargeDatasetDemo
{
    #[State] public string $query = '';

    /**
     * @return array{array<string, string>, int} the first 50 matches, and the
     *                                           number of matches
     */
    public static function search(string $query): array
    {
        $needle = mb_strtolower(trim($query));
        $matches = [];
        $total = 0;
        for ($i = 1; $i <= 10000; ++$i) {
            $name = 'Item '.str_pad((string) $i, 4, '0', \STR_PAD_LEFT);
            if ('' !== $needle && !str_contains(mb_strtolower($name), $needle)) {
                continue;
            }

            ++$total;
            if (\count($matches) < 50) {
                $matches[(string) $i] = $name;
            }
        }

        return [$matches, $total];
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        [$matches, $total] = self::search($this->query);
        $status = $total > 50
            ? 'Showing 50 of '.number_format($total).' items. Type to refine.'
            : null;

        return (
            <Combobox id="items">
                <ComboboxLabel>Search 10,000 items</ComboboxLabel>
                <ComboboxInputGroup>
                    <ComboboxInput phem:bind={{ query }} placeholder="e.g. Item 0042" />
                    <ComboboxActions>
                        <ComboboxClear aria-label="Clear selection" />
                        <ComboboxTrigger aria-label="Open popup" />
                    </ComboboxActions>
                </ComboboxInputGroup>
                <ComboboxPopup>
                    <ComboboxEmpty>No items found.</ComboboxEmpty>
                    <ComboboxList>
                        {% for id, name in matches %}
                            <ComboboxItem key={{ id }} value={{ '' ~ id }}>
                                <ComboboxItemIndicator />
                                <ComboboxItemLabel>{{ name }}</ComboboxItemLabel>
                            </ComboboxItem>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </ComboboxList>
                    <ComboboxStatus className="py-1 pr-5 pl-2 text-sm leading-5 text-neutral-500 empty:hidden dark:text-neutral-400">{{ status }}</ComboboxStatus>
                </ComboboxPopup>
            </Combobox>
        );
    }
}
